id: pm-github-c093
title: "Preserve imported GitHub lifetimes, closure evidence and release attribution while linking cross-provider items"
description: "Repair the import root cause behind twelve Sourcery findings across six gated sync PRs. Preserve source timestamps through supported SDK metadata, map closure reasons and evidence, select tag-date release windows, report state conflicts, and link existing provider owners before creating items. Verify with recorded API fixtures and real temporary trackers at unchanged release gates."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[4]: changelog-unreleased,fidelity,github,import
created_at: "2026-10-16T22:29:39.865Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-17T03:46:54.138Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
comments[19]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-16T22:30:04.918Z",codex-agent,"Read all twelve unresolved Sourcery threads and the changed tracker/changelog files in the six consumer sync PRs. Scope: fix import only; preserve append-only history and leave unrelated closeout work untouched. The pinned SDK exposes completedAt but reserves created_at, updated_at and closed_at; source timestamp metadata plus an explicit SDK-gap receipt is required unless a supported import path proves otherwise. No upstream SDK issue will be filed under the queue rules."
  "2026-10-16T22:35:10.689Z",codex-agent,"Found public SDK import primitives beyond high-level create/update: item locks, canonical document serialization, before/after history entries and appendHistoryEntry. Implementing an idempotent finalization event with real native dates and source metadata, without modifying any historical record. Existing provider owners receive provenance links only; their content, native lifecycle, release and export identity remain authoritative. Local Git calendar tag dates select the first release at or after source closure; later closures remain pending. GraphQL ClosedEvent closer provides actual closing PR attribution where REST commit_id is null."
  "2026-10-16T23:09:24.995Z",codex-agent,"SDK candidate: bulk compensation captures native updated_at and passes it to restore as a history timestamp. Backdating that field disconnects the rollback version from its event. Preserve source creation/closure/completion natively for momentum and cycle time, and retain the exact source update date in github_updated_at while native updated_at stays the SDK mutation clock. Lifecycle finalization now runs at the SDK committing transition before the journal commits, with real compensation acceptance and a post-recovery idempotent check. No historical entries are rewritten."
  "2026-10-16T23:31:39.064Z",codex-agent,"Verified the SDK candidate with a real temporary tracker and public commitImportedItem/commitItemMutations calls: a historical native updated_at followed by an update and deliberate committing failure produces AggregateError, compensation_failed=true, original_restored=false. The importer retains the exact source update timestamp in github_updated_at while keeping native updated_at aligned with immutable event time. Real importer rollback acceptance restores the existing source lifecycle and deletes the newly created item. Focused corrections passed 7/7; final linked tests and unchanged full release gates are running."
  "2026-10-17T00:07:53.005Z",codex-agent,"The source-date, provider-link, privacy-plan and invalid-lifetime targeted checks pass 9/9 after certified SDK corpus reads replaced repeated CLI reads. A real tracker exposed the remaining canceled-to-completed transition: the SDK requires explicit repeat-closure authorization. Import reconciliation uses that supported transition with source closure evidence, and both modes now exercise canceled, completed and reopened states. The earlier release-gate probe had obsolete fixture assumptions and was stopped; final gates will run after these corrections."
  "2026-10-17T00:13:15.552Z",codex-agent,"Terminal reconciliation checks pass 3/3: canceled source records become completed when GitHub does, and reopen clears terminal evidence, in both import modes. Expanded provider matching also follows generic url/external_links when a provider id or tag declares ownership. Final release gates are being restarted against this complete implementation; no coverage thresholds, exemptions or dependency pins changed."
  "2026-10-17T00:22:28.429Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof at implementation 5999329: scratch copies retained the real recorded-API and temporary-tracker tests, rebuilding before each independent function control. Omitting persistImportFidelity yields 9 expected failures across source lifetime fixtures and state-conflict scenarios. Restoring generic importCloseReason wording yields 2 expected failures (beads and slack-standup); dropping linked closure evidence yields 1 (brief closing PR). Tag-only matchImportedIssue yields 2 expected failures (plain and atomic provider owner linking). Clearing buildImportFidelity release attribution yields 1 expected failure in the two-tag before/between/after fixture. Total: 15 expected behavioral failures, zero passes, skips or cancellations; no SDK mocks. Positive targeted checks passed 9/9, terminal transitions 3/3 and expanded identity checks 2/2. Full unchanged release gates remain in progress."
  "2026-10-17T00:27:33.274Z",codex-agent,"The broad gate exposed a real adapter defect for callers passing a repository root: readSettings used the unresolved path, and finalization could append history using a noncanonical item id. Atomic planning now resolves the tracker first; finalization normalizes the id before locking, writing history and invoking hooks. The existing full gate/strict-health fixture and an explicit shortened-id finalization assertion cover this. Updated legacy HTTP replay fixtures to serve closure timelines, and the recovered-journal assertion now expects the earlier explicit no-push refusal. The broad run is diagnostic while these corrections are verified; final release gates will be rerun against frozen source."
  "2026-10-17T00:33:40.746Z",codex-agent,"Canonical-id finalization, both repaired HTTP closure fixtures and recovered-journal refusal pass their targeted assertions. The clean strict-health/push/no-op flow now asserts the correct durable-journal recovery counts and passes; the concurrent two-process race also passes with five distinct comments, keeping the production lock wait and every deduplication assertion unchanged. Refused source cancellation and refused provider-link tests pass 2/2 with real tracker writes, recorded HTTP fixtures and CLI fault boundaries; neither can pass the gate or create a duplicate. Pinned typecheck and test compilation pass. Strict health passes with an isolated global registry; default local health sees a pre-existing shared-registry host-version skew. No dependency or registry changes made. Final PM-linked fixtures and unchanged full release gates are now running against frozen source."
  "2026-10-17T00:39:36.185Z",codex-agent,"Verified all six consumer caller files on their default branches: both reusable workflow SHA and explicit package version remain pinned to 2026.10.16. A new release alone cannot change those pins. Enriched existing adoption task pm-github-aiok rather than creating a duplicate; thread replies will state that the next scheduled sync regenerates the PR after the fixed release is adopted. Consumer branches and workflows remain outside this task."
  "2026-10-17T00:47:09.760Z",codex-agent,"Final PM-linked fixture run at implementation 3d4c1bf passes 26/26 with zero failures, skips, cancellations or TODOs. The command was node_modules/.bin/pm test pm-github-c093 --run --progress, running node --test test/import-fidelity.test.ts on real temporary trackers. Isolated V8 receipts measure import-fidelity.ts at exact 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines. This is module-scoped evidence; package-wide release coverage remains pending. Project policy disables durable test-result capture, so this sanitized comment records the result without changing that policy."
  "2026-10-17T00:50:57.587Z",codex-agent,"Refreshed every behavioral revert control against implementation 3d4c1bf after canonical tracker/id normalization. Each scratch package rebuilt with only the relevant function behavior reverted: lifetimes 9 expected failures, closure wording 2, closing-PR evidence 1, provider identity 2, release attribution 1. All 15 fail for their behavioral assertions, with zero passes, skips or cancellations. The positive 26-case fixture run and module-scoped 100/100/100/100 receipt use the same implementation. Package-wide npm/Bun gates are separate and remain pending."
  "2026-10-17T01:27:07.433Z",codex-agent,"A stronger creation/state-cycle regression exposed completed-journal reuse after state changes. Transaction identity now binds to public immutable history: external edits and earlier different native states invalidate cached completion, while create staging and compensation preserve retry identity. Real SDK checks pass 8/8, including a local reopen, interrupted governed reconciliation, resume, compensation and exact no-op retry. Identity/evidence/history-shape checks pass 4/4: unset provider fields and copied GitHub body/labels cannot change known GitHub ownership; declared nested provider origins and exporter provenance still link existing owners. Closing commit attribution respects the API commit repository URL. Final fixture suite now contains 29 tests; full unchanged gates remain pending."
  "2026-10-17T01:36:22.951Z",codex-agent,"Expanded final PM-linked suite passes 29/29, zero failures, skips, cancellations or TODOs. Fresh V8 receipts again measure import-fidelity.ts at exact 100/100/100/100, including history context selection, direct canceled creation, external local edits, real interrupted reconciliation/resume, nested provider origins, empty-field ownership stability and cross-repository closing commit URLs. Typecheck, test compilation, ESLint, docstrings and zero source duplication pass. The full package npm/Bun gates will now run from the frozen implementation; no thresholds, inventory exclusions, dependency pins or test-result policy changed."
  "2026-10-17T01:42:21.617Z",codex-agent,"Function-only revert proof refreshed against implementation 21b17f3: lifetimes 9 expected failures; closure wording 2; closing-PR evidence 1; provider identity 2; release windows 1; legacy cancellation planning 1; external history revision 1; repeated lifecycle context 1. Total 18 expected failures, zero passes/skips/cancellations. Every package rebuilt first; all 18 failures contain ERR_ASSERTION and no startup/module/syntax failures. The added controls use real SDK trackers to expose stale completed journals and missing cancellation reasons. Positive linked suite passes 29/29; full package gates are running without source changes."
  "2026-10-17T02:06:25.333Z",codex-agent,"The broad gate found one outdated HTTP fixture: the executable clean-publish replay returned issue arrays for closure timeline/GraphQL requests. Updated githubHandler to serve empty closure connections and supplied a valid completed closure date. The focused executable workflow now passes 1/1 through both fresh checkout runs, proving review creation and update. Production source is unchanged from 21b17f3. The running broad pass is collecting remaining coverage feedback before the final npm/Bun reruns."
  "2026-10-17T02:22:19.497Z",codex-agent,"The complete broad pass measures all 14 authored modules at exact 100/100/100/100: 10403/10403 lines and statements, 271/271 functions, 3122/3122 branches. It ran 769 tests: 768 pass, one outdated closure HTTP fixture failed, zero skips/cancellations/TODOs. The repaired executable clean-publish fixture passes 1/1 through both fresh checkouts. This was not a passing release gate. Re-running the literal full npm CI-identity gate and then the Bun release gate with the fixture correction; production source remains 21b17f3."
  "2026-10-17T02:58:38.811Z",codex-agent,"The full CI-identity npm run release:check PASSED at unchanged thresholds: 769/769 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/TODOs, exact 100/100/100/100 across all 14 authored modules. Production dependency audit, package dry-run packing, changelog check and publish attestation passed. Source is still 21b17f3 with the workflow fixture repair in 6cb1a1a. The separate literal bun run release:check is now running sequentially with isolated Git identity and unchanged policy."
  "2026-10-17T03:46:54.138Z",codex-agent,"Both required full release gates PASSED under isolated CI Git identity: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each ran 769/769 tests with zero failures, skips, cancellations or TODOs. Both measured exact 100/100/100/100 across all 14 authored modules at unchanged thresholds: 10403/10403 lines and statements, 271/271 functions, 3122/3122 branches. Audit, package dry-run packing, generated changelog and publish attestation passed. Production source remains 21b17f3; workflow HTTP fixture correction is 6cb1a1a. Preparing the public PR, then checking its CI before replying to the 12 unresolved consumer Sourcery threads."
